  "idea": "Framer vs Webflow: which visual website builder should you build on",
  "text": "Framer feels like Figma alive, while Webflow offers deep CMS and custom code control. Designers often choose Webflow only to get paralyzed by complex class architectures and styling hierarchies. If you only need a modern SaaS landing page, managing nested div blocks destroys creative momentum. Framer provides visual freeform canvas editing, physics-based scroll effects, and instant global hosting. You ship conversion-focused websites twice as fast.",
